{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_cassandra_cassandrajournal", "label": "CassandraJournal", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Shared across cluster nodes, unlike one SQLite file per node, so any node can append or read any persistenceId. The production choice for sharded entities that move between nodes and for cross-node projections; single-node Cassandra is strictly worse than SQLite.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/cassandra.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_cassandra_composite_partition_key", "label": "Composite partition key with bucketing", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Events are keyed by persistence_id and partition_nr and bucketed at partitionSize rows, so a long-lived stream spans multiple partitions and recovery reads one partition per bucket.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/cassandra.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_cassandra_tag_index_table", "label": "events_by_tag side table", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Optional, off by default, partitioned by tag so a projection query hits one partition; each row carries its own copy of the payload.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/cassandra.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_cassandra_compaction_reaches_side_table", "label": "Compaction must reach the side table", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "It is a real dual-written table, not an index Cassandra maintains, and each row holds its own payload copy - so a row left behind would keep answering tag queries and keep storing the body after the event was compacted away. Its keys are not derivable from persistenceId and toSeq, so delete reads the prefix back first.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/cassandra.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_cassandra_consistency_model", "label": "Cassandra journal consistency model", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Within a pid the order is strict by sequenceNr regardless of which replica responds; across pids, tag-query order is timestamp-bound but not strict, so same-timestamp events may interleave.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/cassandra.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_cassandra_lightweight_transactions", "label": "LWT sequence claim on the metadata row", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A CQL INSERT is an upsert, so without the claim two writers reading head N would both pass expectedSeq and both write N+1, the second silently overwriting the first while both callers are told the event persisted. Relational journals cannot lose that race because their primary key rejects the loser.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/cassandra.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_cassandra_lwt_cost", "label": "What the LWT costs", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "One Paxos round trip per append, not per event - roughly 3 to 4 times a plain quorum write. Cross-pid throughput is unaffected since each claim contends only on its own metadata partition. Claiming on metadata is cheaper than IF NOT EXISTS per event, which a conditional batch could not span anyway.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/cassandra.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_cassandra_crash_window_gap", "label": "The claim-before-write crash window", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Claiming first inverts rather than removes the window: a death between the committed claim and the events leaves the head ahead of stored events, a gap. That is the safer trade because a gap is detectable by comparing highestSeq against the highest sequence present, whereas a lost write is not.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/cassandra.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_cassandra_lwt_uniform_across_fleet", "label": "Set lightweightTransactions uniformly", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Cassandra only guarantees LWT linearizability when every write to a partition goes through Paxos, so a rolling change leaving some nodes conditional and others plain breaks the guarantee for the duration of the roll. Sharding aims for one writer per pid but does not guarantee it during a rebalance or split brain.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/cassandra.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_cassandra_identifier_validation", "label": "CQL identifier validation", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Identifiers cannot be bound, so keyspace and table names are interpolated and therefore validated against a strict pattern on every path. Data-center names are CQL string values instead, so they keep hyphens and are quote-escaped; everything else travels as bind parameters.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/cassandra.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_cassandra_serial_consistency_multi_dc", "label": "serialConsistency on a multi-DC keyspace", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The driver default SERIAL is a quorum across every DC, dragging each append over the inter-DC link and undoing what LOCAL_QUORUM buys; LOCAL_SERIAL keeps Paxos inside one DC, at the cost of linearizability only within a DC.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/cassandra.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_cassandra_hot_tag_partitions", "label": "Hot tag partitions", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Every event carrying one tag lands in a single partition, so a blanket audit tag at 10M events a day makes that partition huge; bucket high-volume tags by time window or use finer-grained tags.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/cassandra.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_cassandra_cassandrajournal", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_cassandra_composite_partition_key", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/cassandra.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_cassandra_cassandrajournal", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_cassandra_tag_index_table", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/cassandra.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_cassandra_cassandrajournal", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_cassandra_compaction_reaches_side_table", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/cassandra.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_cassandra_cassandrajournal", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_cassandra_consistency_model", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/cassandra.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_cassandra_cassandrajournal", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_cassandra_lightweight_transactions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/cassandra.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_cassandra_cassandrajournal", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_cassandra_lwt_cost", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/cassandra.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_cassandra_cassandrajournal", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_cassandra_crash_window_gap", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/cassandra.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_cassandra_cassandrajournal", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_cassandra_lwt_uniform_across_fleet", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/sr